{
  "_about": "Open structured data layer (src/open_data/). Per dataset: where it is downloaded from, the source column -> canonical key map (unit, definition tag, year semantics) and the local snapshot it becomes (<TRIPY_DATA_DIR>/derived/open/<dataset>.sqlite, one file per dataset, built by the background job). A column map entry lists the EXACT source spellings it accepts (`source`); the build reads the live header first and matches the spellings case-insensitively (whitespace trimmed) and never guesses: a `required` key (the identity keys) whose spellings are all absent stops that table / file (`schema_mismatch`), an optional key that is absent is recorded in the snapshot meta (`absent_columns`) and its offers are not produced, and two different live columns matching one key are `ambiguous` (stop). `fallback` spellings are read only when no `source` spelling is present. `schema_verified` records whether the map was checked against the live schema; the build re-checks it every time either way. The engine reads only the local snapshots (vPIC: an on-demand decode, cached). `field_map`: the field offers a matched configuration makes, with the definition each source column measures and the route an offer may port to (D-4). Make aliases live in data/identity_vocabulary.json (`open_data_make_aliases`).",
  "version": "open-datasets-v2",
  "snapshot_subdir": "open",
  "refresh_interval_days": 30,
  "datasets": {
